      "role": "user",
      "content": "My bad, I forgot about the attachment thing. Let me just paste the key entries from the database here:\n\n---\nEntry 1: US Patent 9,876,543 (2018) - \"Automated pH Management in Hydroponic Systems\". Describes a system that uses pH sensors to trigger valve sequences for nutrient adjustment.\nEntry 2: US Patent 10,234,567 (2020) - \"Smart Nutrient Dosing\". Focuses on wireless monitoring of nutrient levels in aquatic environments.\nEntry 3: JP Patent 2021/00987 - \"Adaptive Valve Control for Vertical Farming\". Uses feedback loops to adjust flow rates based on sensor input.\n---\n\nSo, looking at Entry 1 specifically, it seems quite close to what my client is doing with their sequence. But I need you to find the angle. Draft that summary for the filing—find the technical nuances that make our client's valve sequence different and more advanced than what's in Entry 1. We need a strong argument for novelty here so we don't get rejected immediately.",
